#!/usr/bin/env bash
# AG_STAGE1_GOVERNANCE_RECONCILIATION_AND_WP7_PREFLIGHT_V1 -- repository-local guard.
#
# Background: a prior task observed commits landing on origin/main without any
# explicit `git push` invocation from that session. Investigation found no repo-local
# git hook responsible; the plausible cause is external to this repository (VS Code's
# global chat.tools.terminal.autoApprove setting pre-approves `git push` for any
# chat/agent tool, and several other agent-capable extensions are installed in this
# same VS Code profile with their own terminal/git access). Neither can be safely
# changed from within this task (they are user/machine-wide, not repository state).
#
# This hook is the safe, minimal, repository-local mitigation available: it makes
# EVERY push through this clone (from any tool, human or agent) require an explicit,
# conscious opt-in via the AG_ALLOW_PUSH environment variable. It does not touch any
# global/user VS Code setting, does not disable any extension, and is fully reversible
# (delete this file, or `git config --unset core.hooksPath`).
#
# To push deliberately:
#   AG_ALLOW_PUSH=1 git push ...
#
# To remove this guard entirely:
#   git config --unset core.hooksPath

if [ "$AG_ALLOW_PUSH" = "1" ]; then
  exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'EOF'
AG_PUSH_BLOCKED_BY_REPOSITORY_LOCAL_GUARD

This repository blocks `git push` by default (scripts/git-hooks/pre-push) after a
prior task observed unexplained automatic commits/pushes to origin/main from this
VS Code workspace (root cause: environment-level auto-approval of git push for
chat/agent tools, not this repository).

To push deliberately, re-run with the explicit opt-in:
    AG_ALLOW_PUSH=1 git push ...

To remove this guard:
    git config --unset core.hooksPath
EOF
exit 1
